    "final_message": "## Summary\n\nI've completed the red acceptance test for the story-drafting user story. Here's what was done:\n\n**Spec**: `<repo>/.baseline-runs/red-v8-haiku-default/spec.toml`\n\nThe spec models a JTBD (job-to-be-done) aggregate with:\n- Identity: `jtbd_id` \n- Fields: `description` (the work being done) and `status` (current step)\n- Operations: `submit_jtbd` (write) and `check_jtbd_status` (read)\n- Workflow: `draft_for_jtbd` orchestrator that should set status to \"drafting\"\n\n**Test**: `<repo>/story-drafting/tests/test_acceptance.py`\n\nClass: `TestSubmitJtbd`, Method: `test_submitted_jtbd_is_drafting`\n\nThe test:\n1. Submits a JTBD via HTTP POST with status=\"pending\" (returns 201 with jtbd_id) \u2705\n2. Checks the status via HTTP GET with the returned ID (returns 200) \u2705\n3. Asserts the status is \"drafting\" \u274c **This fails** \u2014 it's still \"pending\"\n\n**Verification**: `scripts/verify story-drafting` produces:\n- \u2705 tessercheck: zero findings\n- \u2705 mypy --strict: no issues in 57 files\n- \u2705 Tier tests: 56 passed\n- \u2705 HTTP host serves and registers with Restate\n- \u274c Acceptance test fails at the assertion (status is 'pending', expected 'drafting')\n\nThe test correctly fails at the user story's \"then\" (checking that drafting has begun), confirming that the workflow behavior to transition the status is not yet implemented. The test does not fail before that point \u2014 all host operations (submit and read) succeed as expected."
  },
